<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41007" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-mando</span></b> , āre,
			v. a. (late Lat.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To send back word</i>, <i>to notify in
				return</i>, <i><span class="en">Eutr. 2, 13</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Hist. Eccl. 10,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To repeat a command</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manda, remanda,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 28, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">13</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
